        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Social reform targets the conditions of ordinary life rather than the formal structure of political power: who can own property, who gets healthcare, who goes to school, who breathes clean air, whether workers can organize, whether women can vote or own property, whether children labor in mines. These reforms often precede political change, or outlast political upheaval, or happen while political structures remain unchanged."
    },
