      },
      "text": "Examples:\n  - John Snow's cholera map (1854): made the invisible\n    transmission mechanism spatially visible\n  - Harriet Beecher Stowe's Uncle Tom's Cabin: slavery\n    made emotionally real to Northern whites\n  - Rachel Carson's DDT data: made invisible chemical\n    harm measurable and attributable\n  - Nightingale's polar area diagrams: made hospital death\n    rates visible to non-statisticians\n  - Lewis Hine's child labor photographs (1908-1918):\n    made children in mines/factories visible to reformers"
